      "text": "To find out how many minutes it will take for the printer to print 200 pages, we need to divide the total number of pages by the number of pages the printer can print per minute.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Time (minutes)} = \\frac{\\text{Total pages}}{\\text{Pages per minute}} = \\frac{200}{17}\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Calculation\ntotal_pages = 200\npages_per_minute = 17\n\n# Time in minutes\ntime_minutes = total_pages / pages_per_minute\ntime_minutes_rounded = round(time_minutes)\n\nprint((time_minutes, time_minutes_rounded))\n```\n```output\n(11.764705882352941, 12)\n```\nThe calculation shows that it will take approximately \\(11.76\\) minutes to print 200 pages. Rounding this to the nearest whole number, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{12}\n\\]",
